pybind11 >= 3.0.3 returns `typing::Tuple<Args...>` from `py::make_tuple` (PyTorch 2.10.0 bundles 3.0.1, the
easyconfig uses pybind11 3.0.4 via USE_SYSTEM_PYBIND11), so lambdas and `?:` expressions returning tuples of
different element types no longer compile:
> torch/csrc/jit/python/init.cpp:1833:32: error: inconsistent types 'pybind11::typing::Tuple<pybind11::none, pybind11::none>'
>   and 'pybind11::typing::Tuple<pybind11::cpp_function&, pybind11::list&>' deduced for lambda return type
> torch/csrc/utils/python_arg_parser.cpp:763:7: error: operands to '?:' have different types
>   'pybind11::typing::Tuple<pybind11::handle, pybind11::handle>' and 'pybind11::typing::Tuple<pybind11::handle, pybind11::handle, pybind11::handle>'
> torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/init.cpp:897:36: error: inconsistent types ... deduced for lambda return type
Add explicit return types.

Upstream commit b248ebc17075c0c3ad2b2532970d2ada32b2cf94 (https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/179277),
included in PyTorch 2.12.0; regenerated against the v2.10.0 sources.

